cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BEAST: Gordon Bell Prize for Climate Modeling 2026 submission artifact"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the paper "4D Parallelism Unlocks
  Exascale Bayesian Neural Networks for High-Fidelity Atmospheric Modeling"
  (Kieckhefen et al., 2026), https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2609.12815.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/RAI-SCC/GrandBellbeast"
abstract: >-
  Submission artifact for the 2026 Gordon Bell Prize for Climate Modeling.
  This repository contains the code, configurations, job scripts and
  evaluation pipeline needed to reproduce the results of the paper "4D
  Parallelism Unlocks Exascale Bayesian Neural Networks for High-Fidelity
  Atmospheric Modeling". It trains and evaluates BEAST, a Bayesian Swin
  Transformer that predicts global atmospheric states at 0.25 degree resolution
  and quantifies both aleatoric and epistemic uncertainty, on the JUPITER and
  LUMI supercomputers. The model itself is implemented in the BEAST library
  (https://github.com/RAI-SCC/beast).
keywords:
  - atmospheric forecasting
  - uncertainty quantification
  - exascale computing
  - artificial intelligence
  - domain parallelism
  - sampling parallelism
